                <pb facs="0656" n="644" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg644"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.248/1201¾: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Personal Representative
                        of the President in India</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-25T23:00:00-04:00">April 25, 1942—11
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>161. With reference to your no. 190, April 17, 8 p.m. The President desires that
                    the following message from him be conveyed to Colonel Johnson: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“General Brereton has been fully informed of the reinforcements in
                            airplanes he is to expect in the near future and has been directed to
                            operate under the operational control of the appropriate British
                            commander operating in defense of the eastern coast of India.
                            Roosevelt.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
